                                ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
                                ; PURPOSE
                                ;
                                ; This is a self-contained TIKO .COM program for the TIKI 100 containing:
                                ;
                                ;	1. A transient TIKO loader at 0100H.
                                ;	2. A resident driver assembled for execution at 8000H.
                                ;	3. A 2026 TIKI 100 music player and AY/YM backend.
                                ;	4. The complete Sweet Dreams module embedded.
                                ;
                                ; First invocation:
                                ;	- copies the resident image to 8000H;
                                ;	- preserves the original TIKO vector at FF16H;
                                ;	- initializes the music player;
                                ;	- installs the resident music TSR;
                                ;	- returns to TIKO while music continues.
                                ;
                                ; Second invocation:
                                ;	- mutes AY;
                                ;	- restores the original TIKO vector;
                                ;	- removes the resident hook.
                                ;
                                ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
                                ; 2026 TIKI 100 ADAPTATION
                                ;
                                ; Combines the resident TIKO integration, 125-to-50 Hz music timing,
                                ; TIKI 100 AY-3-8912 output, the noise-transient gate and the embedded
                                ; Sweet Dreams module in one source file.
                                ;
                                ; The underlying Universal PT2/PT3 player core remains credited to
                                ; S.V. Bulba (2004-2007), and the music module retains its original author
                                ; credit below.	This note identifies the TIKI 100 integration/adaptation;
                                ; it does not claim authorship of those original works.
                                ;
                                ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
                                ; TARGET AND TOOLCHAIN
                                ;
                                ; Target computer 	: TIKI 100
                                ; Operating system	: TIKO environment
                                ; CPU			: Z80
                                ; Assembler		: Microsoft MACRO-80 (M80)
                                ; Linker		: Microsoft LINK-80 (L80)
                                ;
                                ; Suggested TIKO build:
                                ;
                                ;	M80 =SWEET/Z
                                ;	L80 SWEET,SWEET/N/E
                                ;
                                ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
                                ; FIXED RESIDENT ENTRY TABLE
                                ;
                                ;	8000H	TSRINT	interrupt hook installed at TIKO FF16H
SWEET							PAGE	1-1


                                ;	8003H	TSRSTP	mute and uninstall
                                ;	8006H	TSRINS	install/init, HL = original FF16H vector
                                ;	8009H	MUSINI	music player initialize
                                ;	800CH	MUSTIK	one music player play tick
                                ;	800FH	MUSMUT	mute
                                ;
                                ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
                                ; INTERRUPT CHAIN AND 50 HZ MUSIC CLOCK
                                ;
                                ; TIKO's resident CTC channel-3 vector is at FF16H.
                                ; The interrupt rate is approximately 125 Hz.	The resident hook always
                                ; chains to the vector that was present before installation.
                                ;
                                ; The music player runs on a private 256-byte resident stack rather than on
                                ; the interrupted program's stack.	Both main and alternate Z80 register
                                ; sets are preserved.
                                ;
                                ; The 125 Hz stream is converted to a 50 Hz music player clock with:
                                ;
                                ;	phase = phase + 2
                                ;	if phase >= 5:
                                ;	phase = phase - 5
                                ;	play one music player tick
                                ;
                                ; This gives 16/24 ms spacing and a 20 ms average music player frame period.
                                ;
                                ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
                                ; TIKI 100 AY-3-8912 PSG BACKEND
                                ;
                                ; The tested backend writes the music player register image to TIKI 100 sound ports
                                ; 16H and 17H, in ABC channel order.	The one-frame noise transient gate shortens noise-only
                                ; events; ordinary tone, bass and synth paths are not intentionally altered.
                                ;
                                ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
                                ; MUSIC PLAYER
                                ;
                                ; Core player:
                                ;	Universal PT2/PT3 player by S.V. Bulba, 2004-2007.
                                ;
                                ; Fixed configuration in this edition:
                                ;	PT3 only		= yes
                                ;	register calculator	= yes
                                ;	channel order		= ABC
                                ;	loop checker		= disabled
                                ;	current position	= disabled
                                ;	player identifier	= disabled
                                ;
                                ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
                                ; SWEET DREAMS MODULE
                                ;
                                ; Title		: Sweet Dreams
                                ; Module title: "Sweet Dreams" Eurythmics (rmx)
                                ; PT3 author	: nq/skrju, 211211
                                ; Year		: 2011
                                ; Format	: PT3
                                ; Chip		: AY-compatible
